description:
The general objective of this procurement is to provide high-quality survey fieldwork services enabling the JRC to collect behavioural evidence on how alternative regulatory approaches affect AI adoption decisions among firms in the European Union, with specific attention to rural-urban heterogeneity. The specific objectives are:
1.	to programme and implement a survey questionnaire developed by the JRC, including embedded randomised experimental treatments;
2.	to recruit and survey a representative sample of senior decision-makers in firms across at least three EU Member States;
3.	to ensure sufficient representation of rural firms to permit rigorous subgroup analysis;
4.	to deliver clean, anonymised, well-documented datasets suitable for advanced statistical analysis by the JRC;
5.	to implement all fieldwork in accordance with EU data protection legislation and professional standards for survey research.

The purpose of the contract is to provide the following main category of services related to operating, updating, and/or expanding the “New European Bauhaus Hub for Results and Impacts” 
1.	Collection, management and valorisation of knowledge, results, approaches and solutions which result from NEB projects and initiatives;
2.	Monitor and curate NEB-related academic studies, knowledge, results, approaches, and solutions;
3.	Digital platform management – continuous improvement, maintenance and expansion of an online platform; 
4.	Contribute to the development of an assessment framework to contribute to measure the effects of NEB projects, and to the collection of such evidence;
5.	Policy advisory and stakeholder engagement.

