This contract has the objective of carrying out a survey among dairy farmers to obtain data allowing JRC-IPTS to perform quantitative analysis on the effects of contracting and unfair trading practices UTPs on farm performance. The overall objectives of the contract are:
To collect raw data:
1. on the production information and structure of dairy farmers;
2. on characteristics of and contract details with the main dairy purchaser;
3. on contractual relations with the main milk purchaser that allows to measure UTPs;
4. about the structure of the market allowing measurement of bargaining power in the food chain;
5. on dairy farmers' cooperation.
To collect basic information about the dairy processing industry collected from secondary sources.

JRC Ispra intends to place a contract for the treatment of its bituminised drums waste stream and associatedradioactive waste aimed at the overall minimisation of the final waste package volume and the minimisation oftotal organic content.
The scope of the contract will include:
a) design and authorisation of the treatment service and the transport of the radioactive waste to/from thecontractor's premises;
b) transport of the drums to the contractor's premises;
c) treatment of the radioactive waste in an external facility;
d) possible transfer of title of some radioactive material for reuse; and
e) packaging and transport of the residuals to JRC Ispra.
It may also include supplementary activities such as characterisation of the waste, conditioning of the residualsincluding supply of final waste package, relevant related supplies and services, and relevant related works andservices that will be evaluated according to the capabilities of the market notably during the dialogue phase
